as Cormann","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10148","person_slug":"mathias-cormann","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michael Forshaw","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10235","person_slug":"michael-forshaw","vote":"no"},{"name":"Michaelia Cash","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10707","person_slug":"michaelia-cash","vote":"no"},{"name":"Mitch Fifield","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10224","person_slug":"mitch-fifield","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Sherry","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10576","person_slug":"nick-sherry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nick Xenophon","party":"Centre Alliance","person_id":"tvfy_10717","person_slug":"nick-xenophon","vote":"no"},{"name":"Nigel Scullion","party":"Country Liberal Party","person_id":"tvfy_10569","person_slug":"nigel-scullion","vote":"no"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Russell Trood","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10640","person_slug":"russell-trood","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"no"}],"name":"Same-Sex Couples - Legislative Changes - 12 month transitional period","noes":45,"question":"This division relates to the Policy _[For equal treatment of same-sex couples](/policies/29)_. The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2009-03-19.11.2) introduced by Greens Senator [Sarah Hanson-Young](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Sarah_Hanson-Young&mpc=Senate&house=senate), which means that it was unsuccessful. The motion was: _That the Senate—_ _(a) notes the appreciation of the gay and lesbian community of the recent passing of the same-sex law reforms;_ _(b) recognises:_ _(i) concerns raised by the gay and lesbian community that isolated and vulnerable members of the community may only become aware of these reforms after 30 March 2009 when [Centrelink](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centrelink)’s education campaign commences, and_ _(c) calls on the Government to revisit the implementation of a 12-month transitional period to ensure individuals currently on a social security payment have sufficient time to readjust to the changes._(Read more about these changes on ABC News [here](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2009-02-19/gay-pensioners-required-to-out-themselves-to/301334) and on Lateline [here](http://www.abc.net.au/pm/content/2008/s2525091.htm).) References","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1634","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2009-03-19/1"}
